/// Synopsis: a `#pause` in a paragraph of its own, with blank lines around it, between two items of a list (`-`, `+`), reveals the second item on the next step, as when glued to the lines (the list is the same on every step): on a slide, in an exercise, inside an `emph-box`, a callout, a column, a list centered as a block (`#align(center, block(align(left)[..]))`, which keeps the markers in place: a list right inside an `align(center)` is a limit, in `sections/pause-limits`), a `pad`, an item of a list, after a `set` rule of the slide and inside a `#[ .. ]` with a rule; two marks in a row count as one gap (the item waits for the third step); a box with a label rebuilt around the glued list keeps its label (red, by its `show` rule).
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
